{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Start with the fund’s own website. Rule 6c-11 generally requires an ETF to disclose its **portfolio holdings** (the securities and weights underlying NAV) each business day before the exchange opens, typically on its website. Check the fund’s “holdings” or “portfolio” page and confirm the date.\n\nThe **portfolio composition file (PCF)** is different: it specifies the securities and quantities in a creation/redemption **basket** for that day. A basket may differ from the fund’s full holdings, and the rule does not require every ETF to make its PCF freely available to the public.\n\nWithout NSCC access, ask the ETF sponsor or its transfer agent/distributor whether it provides PCFs to non-NSCC investors, and request the file for the relevant date and format. Access may be discretionary, delayed, or fee-based; don’t treat a holdings download as a PCF."}}
